      "summary": "Evidence summary: 5 validated structured observations; consult observations and conflicts for supported findings.",
      "observations": [
        {
          "category": "other",
          "statement": "Writing, worldbuilding, atmosphere, and memorable characters are recurring strengths; player feedback repeatedly treats reading and interpreting the peninsula's people and history as the central appeal.",
          "sentiment": "positive",
          "recurrence": "moderate",
          "mention_count": 3,
          "evidence_languages": [
            "russian",
            "non_russian"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "durable",
          "source_ids": [
            "source-002",
            "source-003"
          ],
          "player_feedback_ids": [
            "feedback-001",
            "feedback-003",
            "feedback-004"
          ]
        },
        {
          "category": "structure",
          "statement": "Choices and side quests can meaningfully alter settlements, relationships, and later outcomes, rewarding curiosity and repeated play rather than presenting a single fixed path.",
          "sentiment": "positive",
          "recurrence": "limited",
          "mention_count": 2,
          "evidence_languages": [
            "russian",
            "non_russian"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "durable",
          "source_ids": [
            "source-002",
            "source-003"
          ],
          "player_feedback_ids": [
            "feedback-001",
            "feedback-004"
          ]
        },
        {
          "category": "pacing",
          "statement": "The standard deadline is deliberately pressure-producing rather than universally restrictive: some players find forty days sufficient for most content and value the planning tension, while others find the timer stressful or confusing; Casual removes the deadline.",
          "sentiment": "mixed",
          "recurrence": "moderate",
          "mention_count": 3,
          "evidence_languages": [
            "russian",
            "non_russian"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "durable",
          "source_ids": [
            "source-002",
            "source-004"
          ],
          "player_feedback_ids": [
            "feedback-001",
            "feedback-002",
            "feedback-005"
          ]
        },
        {
          "category": "progression",
          "statement": "Survival meters and resource management can create useful early pressure, but a recent player review reports that money and quest rewards can make those systems substantially less demanding in the middle and late game.",
          "sentiment": "mixed",
          "recurrence": "anecdotal",
          "mention_count": 1,
          "evidence_languages": [
            "non_russian"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "durable",
          "source_ids": [
            "source-003"
          ],
          "player_feedback_ids": [
            "feedback-003"
          ]
        },
        {
          "category": "friction",
          "statement": "The deliberately text-heavy and visually sparse presentation is a trade-off: some players value the book-like form, while others find the amount of reading, names, and limited visual variety tiring or difficult to resume after a break.",
          "sentiment": "mixed",
          "recurrence": "limited",
          "mention_count": 2,
          "evidence_languages": [
            "russian",
            "non_russian"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "durable",
          "source_ids": [
            "source-002",
            "source-003"
          ],
          "player_feedback_ids": [
            "feedback-001",
            "feedback-006"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "conflicts": [
        {
          "statement": "The deadline is the clearest recurring disagreement: it adds route-planning tension for some players but feels needlessly stressful to others, with Casual serving as the no-limit alternative.",
